'' -apppermission IS A JAVA NAME (docs/fasting-android F0): it goes into the manifest's XML as it
'' is, so anything but letters, digits, '_' and '.' (starting with a letter) is refused before
'' anything compiles.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -app -target android-x86_64 -apppermission INTERNET -apppermission bad-name tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0197: '-apppermission bad-name': a permission is a name such as INTERNET or android.permission.INTERNET
